# sapintegrationsuite_api_management_certificate_store_reference (Resource)

A certificate store reference is a name that points at a keystore or truststore of the API
portal. Virtual hosts and target endpoints use the reference instead of the store name, so a
certificate rotation is a change of this pointer: upload a new store, point the reference at
it, and nothing else has to be edited.

**Status:** supported. Backed by `CertificateStoreReferences` of the API portal's
`Management.svc`, with SAP's worked examples for create, read, update and delete.

## Prerequisites

- The `api_management` block in the provider configuration, with the role
  `APIPortal.Administrator`.
- The keystore or truststore itself. Creating a store and uploading certificates into it is a UI
  operation without an API; this resource only points at it.

## Lifecycle

| Operation | What happens |
|---|---|
| Create | Creates the reference to `certificate_store_name`. |
| Read | Reads the store name and type. |
| Update | A changed `certificate_store_name` repoints the reference in place; that is the rotation step. |
| Replacement | Changing `name` creates a new reference. |
| Delete | Deletes the reference, not the store. |

